# NOTICE

superred-claim-openai-agent-injection

This module red-teams an OpenAI Agents SDK agent as a superred SecurityClaim. All
code and the bundled attack payloads are original to this module and licensed MIT
(see LICENSE). No third-party dataset or source is vendored.

## Attack payloads

The illustrative direct prompt-injection payloads in
`src/openai_agent_injection_claim/attacks.py` (5) are original content authored for
this module — canonical injection patterns, not copied from any dataset. They exist
so the claim is runnable and testable out of the box and to seed an optimizer; they
are not a benchmark. Supply your own via `agent_injection_claim(attacks=...)`.

## Framework under test (not vendored)

- OpenAI Agents SDK — https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python (MIT). This
  module and the paired `superred-target-openai-agents` depend on the SDK; no SDK
  code is vendored.

## Citation

When reporting results, describe the agent (instructions, tools, guardrails) and
model used — injection susceptibility depends on all of them and is point-in-time.
